  "name": "Porter Ricks",
  "editorial_article": "Porter Ricks is a pioneering German duo composed of sound artist Thomas Köner and techno producer Andy Mellwig, formed in Berlin in 1994. Named after a character from the 1960s television series Flipper, the project became a cornerstone of the burgeoning mid-90s dub techno movement, distinguishing itself with a uniquely subaquatic and immersive sonic signature. By heavily processing found sounds and applying cavernous, dub-inflected reverb to minimalist rhythmic structures, Porter Ricks created music that felt less like traditional club tracks and more like exploration of alien, oceanic environments.\n\nTheir seminal 1996 debut album, *Biokinetics*, is widely regarded as a masterpiece of the genre, perfectly capturing the aesthetic of early Chain Reaction-era techno. The album’s soundscapes were built upon deep, oscillating basslines and dense textures that bridged the gap between ambient, dub, and minimal techno. Their collaborative work, including the project *Symbiotics* with Techno Animal, further pushed these boundaries by introducing more industrial and experimental noise elements into their rhythmic foundation. Following a significant hiatus, the duo returned with *Anguilla Electrica* in 2017, demonstrating that their commitment to deep, textural, and cinematic electronic music remained as potent as ever. Throughout their active career, Porter Ricks has been instrumental in defining the \"dub techno\" sound, influencing a generation of producers who sought to marry the hypnotic repetition of dance music with the expansive, immersive qualities of sound design and environmental ambient music. Their ability to synthesize static hums and metallic resonance into cohesive, deeply engaging compositions remains their most significant cultural contribution.",
